N:HOW READ (2026-11-11): No source plate exists because this is a new composition. The bar-by-bar compositional audit is: bars 1-2 each begin with one eighth rest and contain seven eighth-note onsets, first E-E-G-A-G-E-D then D-D-E-G-E-D-C; bars 3 and 7 place a rest after four eighth notes and contain seven sung onsets; bars 4 and 8 hold C4 for two beats and leave two beats silent. Bars 5-6 repeat the offbeat-entry shape at a higher melodic peak. Every bar totals eight eighth units, the only pitches are C-D-E-G-A, every leap is a fourth or smaller and the written range is C4-C5.
N:UNCERTAIN: Catchiness, student preference, breath comfort at quarter note = 112, lyric-to-note clarity and the safety/accessibility of each movement cue have not been tested. The pop/funk label describes an intended new arrangement, not a reviewed genre emulation. A second score reader, classroom trial, accessibility review and student listening panel remain required before publication.
